  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Post election violence - Nairobi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Archdiocese of Nairobi is currently playing a major role in managing the humanitarian crisis in Nairobi slums caused by the political impasse.   The post election stalemate and violence has so far left over 250,000 people displaced and averagely 1,000 killed.  Archdiocese of Nairobi is working with other agencies to alleviate hygienic, nutritional, shelter and other basic needs the displaced persons have been deprived of. 

Kariobangi parish serves many slums in Nairobi including Korogocho, Huruma, Gitathuru, Ghetto and Kariobangi centre. There are two churches in the parish, one in Kariobangi and one in Korogocho each having received a high number of IDPs.  The area has a high population density, especially within Korogocho itself.</narrative>
  </description>
